#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#, no-wrap
msgid "Improving Expectation Values: Propagated Noise Absorption (PNA)"
msgstr "Meningkatkan Nilai Jangkaan: Penyerapan Hingar Terpropagat (PNA)"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<OpenInLabBanner notebookPath=\"qiskit-addons/pna/01_generate_noise_mitigating_observable.ipynb\" />\n"
msgstr "<OpenInLabBanner notebookPath=\"qiskit-addons/pna/01_generate_noise_mitigating_observable.ipynb\" />\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In this tutorial, we will learn how to leverage the latest tools in the Qiskit ecosystem to implement a fully customizable, error mitigated workflow. We will introduce the PNA technique and use it to mitigate gate errors. We will also use TREX to mitigate readout errors and post-selection to mitigate errors not captured in the learned noise model.\n"
msgstr "Dalam tutorial ini, kita akan belajar cara memanfaatkan alat terkini dalam ekosistem Qiskit untuk melaksanakan aliran kerja yang boleh disesuaikan sepenuhnya dengan pengurangan ralat. Kita akan memperkenalkan teknik PNA dan menggunakannya untuk mengurangkan ralat get. Kita juga akan menggunakan TREX untuk mengurangkan ralat pembacaan dan pemilihan pasca untuk mengurangkan ralat yang tidak ditangkap dalam model hingar yang dipelajari.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Outline**\n"
"- Give a brief overview of ``PNA``\n"
"- Create a Trotterized quantum circuit and observable. Transpile it to the backend and include post-selection measurements.\n"
"- Use ``samplomatic`` to twirl layers of 2Q gates and measurements. Find unique 2Q layers to reduce noise learning cost.\n"
"- Use ``NoiseLearnerV3`` to learn the error model affecting the 2Q gates and measurements.\n"
"- Use ``qiskit-addon-pna`` to generate a noise-mitigating observable\n"
"- Use ``qiskit-ibm-runtime.Executor`` primitive to generate the raw QPU samples reflecting every shot for every twirling randomization and measured basis\n"
"- Use ``qiskit-addon-utils`` to post-process the data into a mitigated expectation value.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Garis Besar**\n"
"- Berikan gambaran ringkas tentang ``PNA``\n"
"- Cipta litar Trotter kuantum dan observable. Transpail ke Backend dan masukkan ukuran pemilihan pasca.\n"
"- Guna ``samplomatic`` untuk memutar lapisan get 2Q dan ukuran. Cari lapisan 2Q unik untuk mengurangkan kos pembelajaran hingar.\n"
"- Guna ``NoiseLearnerV3`` untuk mempelajari model ralat yang mempengaruhi get 2Q dan ukuran.\n"
"- Guna ``qiskit-addon-pna`` untuk menjana observable yang mengurangkan hingar\n"
"- Guna primitif ``qiskit-ibm-runtime.Executor`` untuk menjana sampel QPU mentah yang mencerminkan setiap shot bagi setiap rawak putar dan asas yang diukur\n"
"- Guna ``qiskit-addon-utils`` untuk memproses data menjadi nilai jangkaan yang telah dikurangkan hingar.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "What is propagated noise absorption (PNA)? {#what-is-propagated-noise-absorption-pna}"
msgstr "Apakah penyerapan hingar terpropagat (PNA)? {#what-is-propagated-noise-absorption-pna}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"***A technique for mitigating gate errors by propagating the observable through the inverse noise channel affecting 2-qubit gates, resulting in a noise-mitigating observable.***\n"
"The 2Q gates in the experiment we want to run will be affected by substantial noise.\n"
"![Noisy experiment](/img/qiskit-addons/images/noisy_expt.png)\n"
"If we learn the noise model, we can apply its inverse and cancel the noise.\n"
"![Noise-mitigated experiment](/img/qiskit-addons/images/noise_mitigated_expt.png)\n"
"Instead of implementing the inverse noise channel by sampling it on the QPU as in PEC, we can implement it classically in the measured observable using Pauli propagation. This results in a more complex observable which, when measured, has the effect of mitigating the learned gate noise.\n"
"![PNA overview](/img/qiskit-addons/images/pna_overview.png)\n"
msgstr ""
"***Teknik untuk mengurangkan ralat get dengan mempropagat observable melalui saluran hingar songsang yang mempengaruhi get 2-qubit, menghasilkan observable yang mengurangkan hingar.***\n"
"get 2Q dalam eksperimen yang ingin kita jalankan akan dipengaruhi oleh hingar yang ketara.\n"
"![Eksperimen beringar](/img/qiskit-addons/images/noisy_expt.png)\n"
"Jika kita mempelajari model hingar, kita boleh menerapkan songsangannya dan membatalkan hingar tersebut.\n"
"![Eksperimen dengan hingar dikurangkan](/img/qiskit-addons/images/noise_mitigated_expt.png)\n"
"Daripada melaksanakan saluran hingar songsang dengan mengambil sampelnya di QPU seperti dalam PEC, kita boleh melaksanakannya secara klasik dalam observable yang diukur menggunakan perambatan Pauli. Ini menghasilkan observable yang lebih kompleks yang, apabila diukur, memberi kesan mengurangkan hingar get yang dipelajari.\n"
"![Gambaran keseluruhan PNA](/img/qiskit-addons/images/pna_overview.png)\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Generate the mirrored Trotter circuit and observable {#generate-the-mirrored-trotter-circuit-and-observable}"
msgstr "Jana litar Trotter yang dicerminkan dan observable {#generate-the-mirrored-trotter-circuit-and-observable}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For this experiment, we will study the time dynamics of a 30-site kicked Ising model on a 1D spin chain. The Hamiltonian considered is:\n"
msgstr "Untuk eksperimen ini, kita akan mengkaji dinamik masa bagi model Ising tertendang 30-tapak pada rantai spin 1D. Hamiltonian yang dipertimbangkan ialah:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "$H = -J\\sum\\limits_{\\langle i,j \\rangle} Z_iZ_j + h\\sum\\limits_iX_i$,\n"
msgstr "$H = -J\\sum\\limits_{\\langle i,j \\rangle} Z_iZ_j + h\\sum\\limits_iX_i$,\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "where $J>0$ describes the coupling of nearest-neighbor spins, $i<j$, and the global transverse field, $h$, is set to $\\frac{\\pi}{8}$. The further $h$ is from a Clifford angle (i.e. $\\theta=n\\frac{\\pi}{2}, n \\in \\mathbb{Z}$), the more difficult it becomes to propagate the anti-noise generators through the circuit.\n"
msgstr "di mana $J>0$ menerangkan gandingan spin jiran terdekat, $i<j$, dan medan melintang global, $h$, ditetapkan kepada $\\frac{\\pi}{8}$. Semakin jauh $h$ dari sudut Clifford (iaitu $\\theta=n\\frac{\\pi}{2}, n \\in \\mathbb{Z}$), semakin sukar untuk mempropagat penjana anti-hingar melalui litar.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For the choice of observable, we will consider the average single-site magnetization, $\\frac{1}{N} \\sum_{i=1}^{N} \\langle z_i \\rangle$, where $N$ is the number of sites.\n"
msgstr "Untuk pilihan observable, kita akan mempertimbangkan purata magnet tapak tunggal, $\\frac{1}{N} \\sum_{i=1}^{N} \\langle z_i \\rangle$, di mana $N$ ialah bilangan tapak.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Quantum circuit diagram](/img/qiskit-addons/pna/01-generate-noise-mitigating-observable/output_1.png)\n"
msgstr "![Rajah litar kuantum](/img/qiskit-addons/pna/01-generate-noise-mitigating-observable/output_1.png)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Next, we will choose a chain of qubits on ``ibm_kingston`` that report low error rates and transpile the circuit to the backend.\n"
msgstr "Seterusnya, kita akan memilih rantai qubit pada ``ibm_kingston`` yang melaporkan kadar ralat rendah dan mentranspail litar ke Backend.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Quantum circuit diagram](/img/qiskit-addons/pna/01-generate-noise-mitigating-observable/output_2.png)\n"
msgstr "![Rajah litar kuantum](/img/qiskit-addons/pna/01-generate-noise-mitigating-observable/output_2.png)\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Twirl the 2-qubit gate layers and measurements and find unique layers {#twirl-the-2-qubit-gate-layers-and-measurements-and-find-unique-layers}"
msgstr "Putar lapisan get 2-qubit dan ukuran serta cari lapisan unik {#twirl-the-2-qubit-gate-layers-and-measurements-and-find-unique-layers}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Here we ensure the pass manager annotates the boxes with ``Twirl`` and ``InjectNoise`` annotations, which allow us to learn the noise which will affect our circuit and associate that noise with its corresponding circuit layer.\n"
msgstr "Di sini kita memastikan pengurus laluan (pass manager) menganotasi kotak dengan anotasi ``Twirl`` dan ``InjectNoise``, yang membolehkan kita mempelajari hingar yang akan mempengaruhi litar kita dan mengaitkan hingar tersebut dengan lapisan litar yang sepadan.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "``enable_gates/enable_measure: True``: Box all 2q gate layers and terminal measurements. Single qubit gates will be left-dressed within the boxes.\n"
msgstr "``enable_gates/enable_measure: True``: Kotakkan semua lapisan get 2q dan ukuran terminal. get qubit tunggal akan dipakaikan di dalam kotak.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "``measure_annotations: all`` Include `Twirl` and `ChangeBasis` annotations on the measurement box\n"
msgstr "``measure_annotations: all`` Masukkan anotasi `Twirl` dan `ChangeBasis` pada kotak ukuran\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "``twirling_strategy: active``: Twirl all active qubits in each box containing entangling gates\n"
msgstr "``twirling_strategy: active``: Pusing semua qubit aktif dalam setiap kotak yang mengandungi get penjalin\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "``inject_noise_targets: gates``: ``InjectNoise`` annotations should be added to all ``Twirl``-annotated boxes containing entangling gates\n"
msgstr "``inject_noise_targets: gates``: Anotasi ``InjectNoise`` perlu ditambah pada semua kotak beranotasi ``Twirl`` yang mengandungi get penjalin\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "``inject_noise_strategy: uniform_modification``: All of the noise layers should be scaled equivalently.\n"
msgstr "``inject_noise_strategy: uniform_modification``: Semua lapisan hingar perlu diskala secara setara.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Quantum circuit diagram](/img/qiskit-addons/pna/01-generate-noise-mitigating-observable/output_3.png)\n"
msgstr "![Rajah litar kuantum](/img/qiskit-addons/pna/01-generate-noise-mitigating-observable/output_3.png)\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Generate the template circuit and samplex, define how the circuit will be sampled {#generate-the-template-circuit-and-samplex-define-how-the-circuit-will-be-sampled}"
msgstr "Jana litar templat dan samplex, tentukan cara litar akan disampling {#generate-the-template-circuit-and-samplex-define-how-the-circuit-will-be-sampled}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Here we also add spectator and post-selection measurements, which are needed to perform post-selection on the samples output from ``Executor``.\n"
msgstr "Di sini kita juga menambah ukuran spektator dan pemilihan pasca, yang diperlukan untuk melakukan pemilihan pasca pada sampel output dari ``Executor``.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Quantum circuit diagram](/img/qiskit-addons/pna/01-generate-noise-mitigating-observable/output_4.png)\n"
msgstr "![Rajah litar kuantum](/img/qiskit-addons/pna/01-generate-noise-mitigating-observable/output_4.png)\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Learn the noise {#learn-the-noise}"
msgstr "Pelajari hingar {#learn-the-noise}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Before we run the experiments, we learn the noise model affecting the entangling gates and measurements in the circuit. Having an accurate noise model is necessary to effectively mitigate error. Learning the noise just before executing the experiments gives the best chance of the noise model faithfully describing the actual noise affecting the gates during execution.\n"
msgstr "Sebelum kita menjalankan eksperimen, kita mempelajari model hingar yang mempengaruhi get penjalin dan ukuran dalam litar. Mempunyai model hingar yang tepat adalah perlu untuk mengurangkan ralat dengan berkesan. Mempelajari hingar sejurus sebelum melaksanakan eksperimen memberi peluang terbaik agar model hingar menggambarkan hingar sebenar yang mempengaruhi get semasa pelaksanaan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Before we learn the noise, we need to find the unique 2-qubit layers in our circuit, so we can minimize the number of shots needed to learn the noise for the entire circuit. We use ``find_unique_box_instructions`` from ``samplomatic`` to provide us the unique layers from the boxed circuit, including the measurement layer. These are the layers we pass to the noise learner.\n"
msgstr "Sebelum kita mempelajari hingar, kita perlu mencari lapisan 2-qubit unik dalam litar kita, supaya kita boleh meminimumkan bilangan shot yang diperlukan untuk mempelajari hingar bagi keseluruhan litar. Kita menggunakan ``find_unique_box_instructions`` dari ``samplomatic`` untuk mendapatkan lapisan unik dari litar berkotak, termasuk lapisan ukuran. Lapisan-lapisan inilah yang kita hantar ke pemelajar hingar.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Once we know the layers, we can learn the noise. There are a few parameters we consider:\n"
msgstr "Setelah kita mengetahui lapisan-lapisan tersebut, kita boleh mempelajari hingar. Terdapat beberapa parameter yang perlu dipertimbangkan:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`num_randomizations`: The number of random circuits to use per learning circuit configuration\n"
msgstr "`num_randomizations`: Bilangan litar rawak yang digunakan per konfigurasi litar pembelajaran\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`shots_per_randomization`: Total number of shots to use per random learning circuit\n"
msgstr "`shots_per_randomization`: Jumlah shot yang digunakan per litar pembelajaran rawak\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`layer_pair_depths`: The circuit depths (measured in number of pairs) to use in learning experiments.\n"
msgstr "`layer_pair_depths`: Kedalaman litar (diukur dalam bilangan pasangan) yang digunakan dalam eksperimen pembelajaran.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`post_selection`: We will use edge-based post-selection during learning using `rx` gates to implement the post-measurement pulses\n"
msgstr "`post_selection`: Kita akan menggunakan pemilihan pasca berasaskan tepi semasa pembelajaran menggunakan get `rx` untuk melaksanakan denyutan pasca-ukuran\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Plot output](/img/qiskit-addons/pna/01-generate-noise-mitigating-observable/output_5.png)\n"
msgstr "![Output plot](/img/qiskit-addons/pna/01-generate-noise-mitigating-observable/output_5.png)\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Associate circuit boxes with learned noise {#associate-circuit-boxes-with-learned-noise}"
msgstr "Kaitkan kotak litar dengan hingar yang dipelajari {#associate-circuit-boxes-with-learned-noise}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Here, we create a mapping between the ``InjectNoise`` reference IDs of each box to the learned noise model (`PauliLindbladMap`) affecting the entangling gates in that box.\n"
msgstr "Di sini, kita buat pemetaan antara ID rujukan ``InjectNoise`` bagi setiap kotak kepada model hingar yang dipelajari (`PauliLindbladMap`) yang mempengaruhi get-get belitan dalam kotak tersebut.\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Propagate the observable through the learned anti-noise to get a noise-mitigating observable {#propagate-the-observable-through-the-learned-anti-noise-to-get-a-noise-mitigating-observable}"
msgstr "Sebarkan observable melalui anti-hingar yang dipelajari untuk mendapatkan observable pengurang hingar {#propagate-the-observable-through-the-learned-anti-noise-to-get-a-noise-mitigating-observable}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "As discussed above, this is done in two steps. First, we propagate an anti-noise generator to the end of the circuit. After that, we propagate the observable through that evolved generator. This process is repeated for each anti-noise generator in the circuit. In this implementation, each generator in a given layer is propagated to the end of the circuit in parallel. Additionally, Python multiprocessing is used to perform both the forward-propagation of the anti-noise as well as the back-propagation of the observable in parallel. This prevents a pile-up of evolved generators in memory and also maximizes compute resources.\n"
msgstr "Seperti yang dibincangkan di atas, ini dilakukan dalam dua langkah. Pertama, kita sebarkan penjana anti-hingar ke penghujung litar. Selepas itu, kita sebarkan observable melalui penjana yang telah berkembang itu. Proses ini diulang bagi setiap penjana anti-hingar dalam litar. Dalam pelaksanaan ini, setiap penjana dalam lapisan tertentu disebarkan ke penghujung litar secara selari. Selain itu, pemprosesan berbilang Python digunakan untuk melakukan penyebaran ke hadapan anti-hingar serta penyebaran ke belakang observable secara selari. Ini mencegah penumpukan penjana yang telah berkembang dalam ingatan dan juga memaksimumkan sumber pengiraan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "When running PNA, you will always need to provided a noisy circuit and observable. If your noisy circuit is a boxed circuit with `InjectNoise` annotations, you will need to provide the mapping we created in the step above. One can also pass a non-boxed circuit containing ``PauliLindbladError`` instructions from ``qiskit-aer``. In that case, ``refs_to_noise_models`` does not need to be provided. In addition to the primary inputs, users will want to consider:\n"
msgstr "Apabila menjalankan PNA, anda perlu sentiasa menyediakan litar berderau dan observable. Jika litar berderau anda ialah litar berkotak dengan anotasi `InjectNoise`, anda perlu menyediakan pemetaan yang kita buat dalam langkah di atas. Seseorang juga boleh menghantar litar tanpa kotak yang mengandungi arahan ``PauliLindbladError`` daripada ``qiskit-aer``. Dalam kes itu, ``refs_to_noise_models`` tidak perlu disediakan. Selain input utama, pengguna perlu mempertimbangkan:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`max_err_terms`: The number of terms to keep in each anti-noise generator as it is forward-propagated. Allowing this to be larger generally increases accuracy, but this behavior is not guaranteed to be monotonic.\n"
msgstr "`max_err_terms`: Bilangan sebutan yang dikekalkan dalam setiap penjana anti-hingar semasa ia disebarkan ke hadapan. Membenarkan nilai ini lebih besar secara amnya meningkatkan ketepatan, tetapi kelakuan ini tidak dijamin bersifat monoton.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`max_obs_terms`: The number of terms to keep in the noise-mitigating observable, $\\tilde{O}$, as it is back-propagated through the evolved anti-noise. Larger values generally increase accuracy, but it is not guaranteed to do so monotonically.\n"
msgstr "`max_obs_terms`: Bilangan sebutan yang dikekalkan dalam observable pengurang hingar, $\\tilde{O}$, semasa ia disebarkan ke belakang melalui anti-hingar yang telah berkembang. Nilai yang lebih besar secara amnya meningkatkan ketepatan, tetapi tidak dijamin berlaku secara monoton.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`num_processes`: The number of cores to dedicate to the process. Remember, the generators are forward-propagated and applied to the observable in parallel.\n"
msgstr "`num_processes`: Bilangan teras yang diperuntukkan untuk proses ini. Ingat, penjana disebarkan ke hadapan dan digunakan pada observable secara selari.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`search_step`: The back-propagation step uses a greedy method to approximately conjugate two operators in the Pauli basis. This method can be sped up by increasing ``search_step``. See the [pauli-prop docs](https://qiskit.github.io/pauli-prop/) for more info.\n"
msgstr "`search_step`: Langkah penyebaran ke belakang menggunakan kaedah tamak untuk mengkonjugat secara anggaran dua pengoperasi dalam asas Pauli. Kaedah ini boleh dipercepatkan dengan meningkatkan ``search_step``. Lihat [dokumentasi pauli-prop](https://qiskit.github.io/pauli-prop/) untuk maklumat lanjut.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`num_to_measure`: While this variable isn't an input to ``generate_noise_mitigating_observable``, we use it to control how many terms from $\\tilde{O}$ we actually want to measure. Here we will only measure the top 30 terms, which are the original terms in our observable. The terms have now been re-scaled such that measuring them has the effect of mitigating the learned gate noise. Although we only measure 30 terms from $\\tilde{O}$, it is often still useful to allow it to grow large, as that increases the precision of the leading terms' scaling factors.\n"
msgstr "`num_to_measure`: Walaupun pemboleh ubah ini bukan input kepada ``generate_noise_mitigating_observable``, kita gunakannya untuk mengawal berapa banyak sebutan daripada $\\tilde{O}$ yang sebenarnya kita mahu ukur. Di sini kita hanya akan mengukur 30 sebutan teratas, iaitu sebutan asal dalam observable kita. Sebutan-sebutan tersebut kini telah diskalakan semula supaya mengukurnya mempunyai kesan mengurangkan hingar get yang dipelajari. Walaupun kita hanya mengukur 30 sebutan daripada $\\tilde{O}$, seringkali masih berguna untuk membiarkannya berkembang besar, kerana itu meningkatkan ketepatan faktor penskalaan sebutan-sebutan terdepan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Plot output](/img/qiskit-addons/pna/01-generate-noise-mitigating-observable/output_6.png)\n"
msgstr "![Plot output](/img/qiskit-addons/pna/01-generate-noise-mitigating-observable/output_6.png)\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Transform the measurement bases to canonical form {#transform-the-measurement-bases-to-canonical-form}"
msgstr "Ubah asas pengukuran ke bentuk kanonik {#transform-the-measurement-bases-to-canonical-form}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Next, we will find a minimal set of bases to measure such that we can fully cover every Pauli term in the measured observable (***many observables may be measured simultaneously if they commute qubit-wise***). Since we are only measuring the terms in our original observable, which is the sum of all single-`Z` Paulis, a single basis is needed -- the all-`Z` basis.\n"
msgstr "Seterusnya, kita akan mencari set asas minimum untuk diukur supaya kita dapat meliputi sepenuhnya setiap sebutan Pauli dalam observable yang diukur (***banyak observable boleh diukur serentak jika ia komut secara qubit-wise***). Memandangkan kita hanya mengukur sebutan dalam observable asal kita, iaitu jumlah semua Pauli tunggal-`Z`, hanya satu asas diperlukan -- asas semua-`Z`.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In addition to finding a set of Pauli measurement bases, we need to map these Pauli terms to the canonical form expected by the ``Executor`` primitive. For more information on canonical qubit ordering, visit the [samplomatic docs](https://qiskit.github.io/samplomatic/guides/samplex_io.html#qubit-ordering-convention).\n"
msgstr "Selain mencari set asas pengukuran Pauli, kita perlu memetakan sebutan-sebutan Pauli ini ke bentuk kanonik yang dijangkakan oleh primitif ``Executor``. Untuk maklumat lanjut tentang pengaturan qubit kanonik, layari [dokumentasi samplomatic](https://qiskit.github.io/samplomatic/guides/samplex_io.html#qubit-ordering-convention).\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Specify how to sample in the ``QuantumProgram`` {#specify-how-to-sample-in-the-quantumprogram}"
msgstr "Tentukan cara pensampelan dalam ``QuantumProgram`` {#specify-how-to-sample-in-the-quantumprogram}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The ``QuantumProgram`` is where we specify how to sample the experiment:\n"
msgstr "``QuantumProgram`` adalah tempat kita menentukan cara untuk mensampel eksperimen:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "``template_circuit``: The circuit containing all the gates necessary to implement all desired randomizations (from twirling randomizations, parameters, etc).\n"
msgstr "``template_circuit``: Litar yang mengandungi semua get yang diperlukan untuk melaksanakan semua rawak yang dikehendaki (daripada rawak twirling, parameter, dll.).\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "``samplex``: An object definining a probability distribution over all possible circuit randomizations from which to sample.\n"
msgstr "``samplex``: Objek yang mendefinisikan taburan kebarangkalian ke atas semua kemungkinan rawak litar untuk disampel.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "``samplex_arguments``: Bindings necessary to fully define the samplex\n"
msgstr "``samplex_arguments``: Pengikatan yang diperlukan untuk menentukan samplex sepenuhnya\n"

#. type: Bullet: '    - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "``basis_changes``: Here is where we specify a set of bases to measure which will cover all of the Pauli terms in the measured observable.\n"
msgstr "``basis_changes``: Di sinilah kita menentukan set asas untuk diukur yang akan meliputi semua sebutan Pauli dalam observable yang diukur.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '    - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "``noise_scales.ref``: We set each noise layer's scale to `0.0` to prevent any additional noise from being injected into our samples\n"
msgstr "``noise_scales.ref``: Kita tetapkan skala setiap lapisan hingar kepada `0.0` untuk mencegah hingar tambahan daripada disuntik ke dalam sampel kita\n"

#. type: Bullet: '    - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "``pauli_lindblad_maps``: Required if ``noise_scales`` are passed. This just maps noise layers to the associated noise model.\n"
msgstr "``pauli_lindblad_maps``: Diperlukan jika ``noise_scales`` dihantar. Ini hanya memetakan lapisan hingar kepada model hingar yang berkaitan.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "``shape``: A shape tuple to extend the implicit shape defined by ``samplex_arguments``. Non-trivial axes introduced by this extension enumerate randomizations.\n"
msgstr "``shape``: Tupel bentuk untuk melanjutkan bentuk implisit yang ditakrifkan oleh ``samplex_arguments``. Paksi bukan trivial yang diperkenalkan oleh pelanjutan ini menghitung rawak.\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Sample the circuit using the ``Executor`` primitive prototype {#sample-the-circuit-using-the-executor-primitive-prototype}"
msgstr "Sampel litar menggunakan prototaip primitif ``Executor`` {#sample-the-circuit-using-the-executor-primitive-prototype}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Now that we have defined our ``QuantumProgram``, executing the experiment is straightforward. We simply instantiate the ``Executor`` object, provide it the backend, and run the program.\n"
msgstr "Setelah kita mendefinisikan ``QuantumProgram``, melaksanakan eksperimen adalah mudah. Kita hanya perlu membuat instantiasi objek ``Executor``, menyediakan Backend, dan menjalankan program.\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Post-process the samples to calculate an error-mitigated expectation value {#post-process-the-samples-to-calculate-an-error-mitigated-expectation-value}"
msgstr "Proses pasca sampel untuk mengira nilai jangkaan termitigasi ralat {#post-process-the-samples-to-calculate-an-error-mitigated-expectation-value}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To calculate an error-mitigated expectation value, we will:\n"
msgstr "Untuk mengira nilai jangkaan termitigasi ralat, kita akan:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Calculate the TREX scaling factors based on the learned noise affecting the measurements\n"
msgstr "Mengira faktor penskalaan TREX berdasarkan hingar yang dipelajari yang mempengaruhi pengukuran\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Generate a mask for keeping only post-selected samples\n"
msgstr "Menjana topeng untuk mengekalkan hanya sampel terpilih pasca\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Use the ``executor_expectation_values`` function from ``qiskit-addon-utils`` for combining all of the data into an error-mitigated expectation value.\n"
msgstr "Menggunakan fungsi ``executor_expectation_values`` daripada ``qiskit-addon-utils`` untuk menggabungkan semua data menjadi nilai jangkaan termitigasi ralat.\n"

